-- Vietnam deep-dive content (English). Vietnam is the second addition
-- from the Asia-Pacific coverage evaluation (South Korea was first).
-- Vietnam's mandate is genuinely dual-model: an invoice either carries
-- a GDT-issued code obtained before delivery (real-time clearance,
-- the same shape as Jordan/Israel/Egypt elsewhere in this tracker) or
-- transmits to the GDT no later than the same day without a code (the
-- same shape as South Korea's post-issuance reporting model). Rather
-- than force one framing, this content describes both flows as two
-- separate lifecycle pill cards, per the Malaysia precedent of
-- multiple genuinely-distinct pill-list cards in one section. The
-- penalty schedule is also structurally different from every prior
-- country: fines escalate by the *count* of violating invoices within
-- an inspection period, not by a flat or percentage figure, following
-- Decree 310/2025/ND-CP (effective 16 January 2026).










